1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,650
[Disclaimer:
All depicted events are fictional

2
00:00:01,680 --> 00:00:03,390
and for entertainment purposes only;
viewer discretion is advised]

3
00:00:12,100 --> 00:00:17,440
[Your Third Series]

4
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:21,670
I'm turning 23 this year.

5
00:00:21,700 --> 00:00:23,030
It's not my unlucky year yet,

6
00:00:23,070 --> 00:00:26,010
but it seems like my life
is constantly being tested.

7
00:00:26,210 --> 00:00:27,540
I can speak five languages,

8
00:00:27,580 --> 00:00:29,810
going global like a diplomat's son.

9
00:00:29,840 --> 00:00:32,900
I've done all sorts of extreme activities,

10
00:00:32,930 --> 00:00:37,110
and now, I'm working as an assistant secretary
for Mr. Sib, Sattawat Adisuan,

11
00:00:37,140 --> 00:00:40,890
an executive at
a top-tier consumer goods manufacturer.

12
00:00:40,930 --> 00:00:41,620
Drowning?

13
00:00:41,910 --> 00:00:42,520
I will surface.

14
00:00:42,640 --> 00:00:43,300
Burning?

15
00:00:43,320 --> 00:00:44,020
I won't get burnt.

16
00:00:44,080 --> 00:00:45,050
Getting hit by a truck?

17
00:00:45,120 --> 00:00:45,920
I can dodge it.

18
00:00:45,960 --> 00:00:46,680
Lost in the woods?

19
00:00:46,710 --> 00:00:48,380
I have my own GPS.

20
00:00:48,410 --> 00:00:49,520
It's built into my watch.

21
00:00:49,620 --> 00:00:51,360
I'm prepared for any situation.

22
00:00:52,950 --> 00:00:53,910
You speak five languages?

23
00:00:54,160 --> 00:00:54,770
Indeed.

24
00:00:54,810 --> 00:00:55,360
Thai?

25
00:00:55,520 --> 00:00:56,420
Hello.

26
00:00:56,750 --> 00:00:59,040
My name is Jam. It's nice to meet you.

27
00:00:59,150 --> 00:00:59,680
Chinese?

28
00:00:59,730 --> 00:01:01,720
Hello. My name is Jam.

29
00:01:01,800 --> 00:01:03,240
It's a pleasure to meet you.

30
00:01:03,440 --> 00:01:04,200
English?

31
00:01:04,319 --> 00:01:05,960
Hello, my name is Jam.

32
00:01:06,040 --> 00:01:07,160
Nice to meet you.

33
00:01:07,360 --> 00:01:08,039
Spanish?

34
00:01:08,280 --> 00:01:10,180
Hello. My name is Jam.

35
00:01:10,300 --> 00:01:11,640
Pleased to meet you.

36
00:01:12,000 --> 00:01:12,840
Japanese?

37
00:01:12,930 --> 00:01:16,039
Hello. My name is Jam.

38
00:01:16,190 --> 00:01:18,950
I'm eager to learn from you.

39
00:01:21,850 --> 00:01:23,620
On top of that, I am a really fast learner.

40
00:01:36,680 --> 00:01:39,759
[Adisuan Group]

41
00:01:43,900 --> 00:01:46,080
Welcome to 'Adisuan Group.'

42
00:01:47,280 --> 00:01:48,289
Thank you.

43
00:01:55,720 --> 00:01:57,080
[Mr. Sib]

44
00:01:57,180 --> 00:01:57,780
Mr. Sib.

45
00:01:59,300 --> 00:02:00,180
Yes, Mr. Sib?

46
00:02:00,200 --> 00:02:02,110
My husband has been hospitalized
due to a seafood allergy.

47
00:02:02,210 --> 00:02:03,120
Please take over for me.

48
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:03,970
No problem.

49
00:02:06,700 --> 00:02:07,790
Mr. PiMai.

50
00:02:12,200 --> 00:02:13,790
Hello, Mr. Jam.

51
00:02:15,210 --> 00:02:16,920
Hello, Mr. PiMai.

52
00:02:17,060 --> 00:02:18,060
Was the trip here rough?

53
00:02:18,320 --> 00:02:19,320
It wasn't at all.

54
00:02:20,230 --> 00:02:22,710
From what I saw on soap operas...

55
00:02:23,200 --> 00:02:23,810
Have you eaten yet?

56
00:02:23,840 --> 00:02:26,590
I thought a boss's spouse
must be fussy and get agitated easily.

57
00:02:26,660 --> 00:02:27,620
I have.

58
00:02:27,930 --> 00:02:29,720
However, Mr. PiMai is such a sweetheart

59
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:31,520
and is surprisingly soft and kind.

60
00:03:00,100 --> 00:03:00,640
Mr. Sib?!

61
00:03:01,630 --> 00:03:03,190
Where is PiMai staying in Chiang Mai?

62
00:03:03,230 --> 00:03:04,920
I need an answer in five minutes.

63
00:03:04,960 --> 00:03:05,840
Understood!

64
00:03:10,120 --> 00:03:11,570
PiMai has a wrist injury.

65
00:03:11,610 --> 00:03:13,110
Keep him company for a bit, can you?

66
00:03:13,140 --> 00:03:14,800
Take this as a change of pace.

67
00:03:15,020 --> 00:03:16,130
Yes, Mr. Sib.

68
00:03:16,210 --> 00:03:17,990
Am I his assistant secretary

69
00:03:18,040 --> 00:03:20,020
or his superhero on demand?

70
00:03:21,240 --> 00:03:21,920
Mr. Jam?

71
00:03:22,050 --> 00:03:23,240
Can you wrap your own wrist?

72
00:03:23,810 --> 00:03:25,280
Is your wrist still hurting?

73
00:03:25,310 --> 00:03:25,930
Uh...

74
00:03:26,440 --> 00:03:28,000
Well... It still kind of is.

75
00:03:28,170 --> 00:03:29,880
I hope you get well soon.

76
00:03:33,360 --> 00:03:35,940
[Adisuan Group]

77
00:03:35,970 --> 00:03:36,930
Take a seat, Mr. Jam.

78
00:03:37,050 --> 00:03:37,930
Thank you.

79
00:03:47,090 --> 00:03:50,040
Lately, Adisuan Group
has been losing its footing.

80
00:03:51,450 --> 00:03:53,820
"I may disappear for a while.
No need to look for me.

81
00:03:53,890 --> 00:03:56,440
This wounded tiger
needs time to nurse his wounds.

82
00:03:56,610 --> 00:03:57,920
I will return when I am fine."

83
00:04:00,770 --> 00:04:01,770
Take a look at this.

84
00:04:02,430 --> 00:04:03,120
Yes?

85
00:04:09,360 --> 00:04:10,000
That...

86
00:04:10,360 --> 00:04:11,320
It's from my younger brother.

87
00:04:13,100 --> 00:04:14,030
Mr. Sarm?

88
00:04:18,190 --> 00:04:19,720
What happened to him?

89
00:04:21,860 --> 00:04:22,760
Well...

90
00:04:23,130 --> 00:04:25,340
He probably wanted to take his time off, as stated.

91
00:04:28,150 --> 00:04:30,610
Adisuan Farm
has been having problems lately

92
00:04:30,650 --> 00:04:33,680
since its owner has vanished
into thin air for months.

93
00:04:33,710 --> 00:04:35,220
No one knows where he is.

94
00:04:35,440 --> 00:04:36,659
He has abandoned his job.

95
00:04:36,950 --> 00:04:38,400
He probably has forgotten...

96
00:04:38,550 --> 00:04:39,830
what his responsibilities are.

97
00:04:39,960 --> 00:04:42,030
It'd be fine if he was gone for just a while.

98
00:04:42,060 --> 00:04:43,930
But it's been way too long.

99
00:04:44,110 --> 00:04:45,840
Adisuan Group can't simply wait like this.

100
00:04:46,440 --> 00:04:49,150
Should tiny problems go unresolved,

101
00:04:49,840 --> 00:04:52,360
they will cause a domino effect
that ruins everything.

102
00:04:52,770 --> 00:04:54,150
In two weeks,

103
00:04:55,200 --> 00:04:57,040
Namnueng, my sister, is getting married.

104
00:04:59,159 --> 00:05:01,940
She takes the word "family" very seriously.

105
00:05:02,740 --> 00:05:04,330
This means that

106
00:05:04,760 --> 00:05:06,320
all of the siblings must show up.

107
00:05:07,110 --> 00:05:07,930
Mr. Sarm...

108
00:05:08,200 --> 00:05:09,300
must be brought back.

109
00:05:11,530 --> 00:05:13,440
Having worked together,

110
00:05:14,140 --> 00:05:16,550
I'm sure you have strong persuasive skills.

111
00:05:16,690 --> 00:05:19,600
You can easily convince people
and win them over.

112
00:05:19,940 --> 00:05:21,440
This quality of yours is second to none.

113
00:05:21,940 --> 00:05:23,560
Don't say that word, please...

114
00:05:26,850 --> 00:05:27,610
I...

115
00:05:28,130 --> 00:05:29,060
Please, no.

116
00:05:29,420 --> 00:05:31,440
I want you to bring Mr. Sarm back to us.

117
00:05:32,750 --> 00:05:34,500
But you are brothers.

118
00:05:34,530 --> 00:05:36,760
You might have an easier time
convincing him than I do.

119
00:05:38,070 --> 00:05:39,290
You have a group chat.

120
00:05:39,360 --> 00:05:41,340
Please talk to each other, boss...

121
00:05:41,360 --> 00:05:43,820
If I have to do everything with my two hands,

122
00:05:45,060 --> 00:05:46,560
then what's the point of having you around?

123
00:05:58,600 --> 00:05:59,460
Okay.

124
00:06:00,050 --> 00:06:01,650
It's just a special mission.

125
00:06:02,340 --> 00:06:03,850
Let's look on the bright side.

126
00:06:06,440 --> 00:06:07,450
Just thinking about it...

127
00:06:08,950 --> 00:06:10,160
already gives me chills.

128
00:06:14,620 --> 00:06:16,880
Sib, you're not going to kiss your husband?

129
00:06:20,600 --> 00:06:21,650
Kiss him.

130
00:06:21,690 --> 00:06:23,590
Kiss him. Kiss him.

131
00:06:23,700 --> 00:06:25,280
Kiss now. Kiss now.

132
00:06:25,300 --> 00:06:26,860
Kiss him. Kiss him.

133
00:06:26,900 --> 00:06:28,620
Kiss now. Kiss now...

134
00:06:28,650 --> 00:06:30,340
Kiss him...

135
00:06:32,750 --> 00:06:34,100
Kiss him.

136
00:06:34,120 --> 00:06:35,950
Kiss him. Kiss him.

137
00:06:35,970 --> 00:06:38,720
Kiss him now. Kiss him now.

138
00:06:38,740 --> 00:06:40,440
Kiss him. Kiss him.

139
00:06:40,470 --> 00:06:41,830
Kiss now. Kiss now.

140
00:06:53,170 --> 00:06:54,250
Very lovely.

141
00:07:01,920 --> 00:07:02,820
By the way...

142
00:07:02,860 --> 00:07:04,040
Who are you?

143
00:07:06,100 --> 00:07:07,510
My name is Jam,

144
00:07:08,130 --> 00:07:10,080
and I'm Mr. Sib's assistant secretary.

145
00:07:10,820 --> 00:07:12,070
And...

146
00:07:12,090 --> 00:07:13,500
do you know who I am?

147
00:07:14,400 --> 00:07:15,720
If I have to guess...

148
00:07:16,310 --> 00:07:19,080
you must be one of Mr. Sib's twin brothers,

149
00:07:19,240 --> 00:07:22,360
and you are working as a doctor
at Pakchong Hospital, correct?

150
00:07:22,900 --> 00:07:23,820
You are sharp

151
00:07:24,170 --> 00:07:25,280
and quick-witted.

152
00:07:26,170 --> 00:07:27,300
Are you two going to talk all day?

153
00:07:31,860 --> 00:07:32,390
And...

154
00:07:33,600 --> 00:07:34,750
Do you know...

155
00:07:34,770 --> 00:07:35,430
who this guy

156
00:07:35,820 --> 00:07:36,570
actually is?

157
00:07:37,200 --> 00:07:38,720
That is Mr. Sarm,

158
00:07:38,900 --> 00:07:40,880
your younger twin brother, Mr. Song.

159
00:07:41,020 --> 00:07:43,720
He is now in charge of
all of Adisuan Group's operations,

160
00:07:43,900 --> 00:07:45,800
including the gigantic orange orchard

161
00:07:45,840 --> 00:07:47,290
and the food processing factories...

162
00:07:47,320 --> 00:07:48,290
Enough already.

163
00:07:51,010 --> 00:07:52,010
It's annoying.

164
00:08:09,900 --> 00:08:10,880
Good at organizing, huh?

165
00:08:12,510 --> 00:08:13,120
Was it you...

166
00:08:13,290 --> 00:08:15,100
who set them up to be together?

167
00:08:15,490 --> 00:08:16,730
Sarm...

168
00:08:16,900 --> 00:08:18,310
What do you mean I set them up?

169
00:08:18,970 --> 00:08:21,440
Mr. Sib and Mr. PiMai love each other.

170
00:08:21,930 --> 00:08:23,320
And what is it that makes you upset?

171
00:08:23,500 --> 00:08:24,310
Let go!

172
00:08:25,210 --> 00:08:26,600
If you don't want to get hurt,

173
00:08:28,350 --> 00:08:29,640
don't act like you know everything.

174
00:08:34,330 --> 00:08:35,159
Easy now.

175
00:08:36,500 --> 00:08:38,010
Please don't hold it against him.

176
00:08:39,380 --> 00:08:40,520
That's who he is.

177
00:08:41,309 --> 00:08:42,010
Right.

178
00:09:06,360 --> 00:09:07,280
What are you doing here,

179
00:09:07,680 --> 00:09:08,200
Snoop?

180
00:09:08,840 --> 00:09:09,920
I am sorry,

181
00:09:10,100 --> 00:09:12,720
but my name is Jam, not "Snoop."

182
00:09:14,490 --> 00:09:16,880
I am here to pay Mr. PiMai a visit,
as any caring friend would.

183
00:09:16,980 --> 00:09:17,880
When did you two get close?

184
00:09:17,990 --> 00:09:19,160
It's because you're like this.

185
00:09:19,220 --> 00:09:20,790
What else would I call you but "Snoop"?

186
00:09:21,110 --> 00:09:21,800
Wait...

187
00:09:22,440 --> 00:09:23,180
Oh!

188
00:09:23,520 --> 00:09:24,520
How about "Snoopy Jerk"?

189
00:09:24,590 --> 00:09:25,670
Mr. Sarm...

190
00:09:25,800 --> 00:09:27,280
Did Sib send you to spy on things?

191
00:09:27,410 --> 00:09:29,080
I think the reason I'm here...

192
00:09:29,230 --> 00:09:31,360
is of no concern to you.

193
00:09:32,200 --> 00:09:33,160
Quite a sharp tongue.

194
00:09:33,880 --> 00:09:34,720
Know this, you.

195
00:09:34,760 --> 00:09:37,080
As long as you are at Adisuan Farm,

196
00:09:37,170 --> 00:09:39,520
I can release my beaked friends
to peck you whenever I please.

197
00:09:39,580 --> 00:09:41,360
Well, know this, Mr. Sarm.

198
00:09:41,440 --> 00:09:43,570
If I'm harmed in the slightest,

199
00:09:43,600 --> 00:09:45,560
all that will be left here is nothing but ashes.

200
00:09:48,640 --> 00:09:50,090
Oh, you.

201
00:09:50,280 --> 00:09:51,780
Hey, Mr. Sarm!

202
00:09:52,330 --> 00:09:53,640
What did I tell you?

203
00:09:53,920 --> 00:09:55,040
"If you don't want to get hurt,

204
00:09:55,300 --> 00:09:56,480
don't act like you know everything."

205
00:09:56,750 --> 00:09:58,680
I'll tell you one more thing, then.

206
00:09:59,010 --> 00:10:00,360
If you don't want to live a hard life,

207
00:10:00,570 --> 00:10:02,120
then don't act so tough with me.

208
00:10:06,000 --> 00:10:06,640
Beep-beep.

209
00:10:07,010 --> 00:10:09,400
Beep-beep, beep-beep, beep-beep.

210
00:10:15,890 --> 00:10:17,160
Would you like to go bird watching with me?

211
00:10:17,490 --> 00:10:18,250
I would love to.

212
00:10:18,300 --> 00:10:19,410
Don't go too far, alright?

213
00:10:20,200 --> 00:10:20,890
Yes.

214
00:10:21,890 --> 00:10:22,690
Come on.

215
00:10:22,730 --> 00:10:23,360
Let's go.

216
00:10:23,390 --> 00:10:24,320
This way, please.

217
00:10:28,190 --> 00:10:30,000
Birds by the garden...

218
00:10:32,620 --> 00:10:34,100
Don't be dishonest with your feelings.

219
00:10:35,200 --> 00:10:36,810
If you want to follow
your husband, then go.

220
00:10:39,420 --> 00:10:40,890
Let them have fun on their own.

221
00:10:41,510 --> 00:10:42,310
Hey, Sib...

222
00:10:43,010 --> 00:10:44,010
Do you really love PiMai?

223
00:10:45,900 --> 00:10:47,210
If you don't, let him go.

224
00:10:49,440 --> 00:10:51,400
I won't, and I will never.

225
00:10:53,490 --> 00:10:54,810
Just say it already, damn it.

226
00:10:55,020 --> 00:10:56,120
Say it out loud!

227
00:10:56,770 --> 00:10:58,600
Just let me hear it already.

228
00:10:58,890 --> 00:10:59,790
If you don't love him,

229
00:11:01,430 --> 00:11:02,040
let him be mine.

230
00:11:04,950 --> 00:11:06,700
That's for saying without thinking.

231
00:11:08,900 --> 00:11:11,140
And that's for having
nasty thoughts toward my man.

232
00:11:21,300 --> 00:11:22,200
- Mr. Sib!
- Dear Sib...

233
00:11:24,310 --> 00:11:25,620
Did something happen?

234
00:11:26,000 --> 00:11:26,910
It was nothing.

235
00:11:27,900 --> 00:11:29,090
A busted lip isn't gonna kill him.

236
00:11:29,400 --> 00:11:30,170
Into the house.

237
00:11:30,210 --> 00:11:31,090
But Sarm...

238
00:11:39,510 --> 00:11:41,290
It is okay, Mr. Sarm.

239
00:11:42,360 --> 00:11:43,920
It is but a minor injury...

240
00:11:45,170 --> 00:11:46,120
like being stung by ants.

241
00:11:51,070 --> 00:11:51,910
You think we're friends?

242
00:12:00,100 --> 00:12:00,840
Hey!

243
00:12:01,860 --> 00:12:02,710
Drive for me.

244
00:12:04,320 --> 00:12:05,840
You aren't going to do it yourself?

245
00:12:05,950 --> 00:12:06,770
I can't.

246
00:12:06,800 --> 00:12:07,880
My heart's too weak.

247
00:12:08,910 --> 00:12:09,880
That's ridiculous.

248
00:12:09,940 --> 00:12:11,090
What's really wrong with you?

249
00:12:13,080 --> 00:12:14,560
Well, I'm officially heartbroken.

250
00:12:26,920 --> 00:12:27,820
Gosh...

251
00:12:33,020 --> 00:12:34,020
I'm okay.

252
00:12:35,100 --> 00:12:35,960
I'm fine.

253
00:12:37,410 --> 00:12:38,200
Thank you.

254
00:12:43,900 --> 00:12:45,000
Wait for me, please!

255
00:12:48,200 --> 00:12:50,240
All I have to do is bring Mr. Sarm back

256
00:12:50,500 --> 00:12:53,280
for the Outstanding Employee Trophy.

257
00:12:54,990 --> 00:12:57,400
How hard can it be?

258
00:13:19,150 --> 00:13:21,920
Kiss him. Kiss him. Kiss him.

259
00:13:34,210 --> 00:13:35,080
Sarm!

260
00:13:37,030 --> 00:13:38,720
Don't do the unthinkable, Sarm!

261
00:13:42,620 --> 00:13:44,240
Please don't die, Sarm!

262
00:13:49,320 --> 00:13:50,400
Sarm!

263
00:13:56,400 --> 00:13:57,500
Sarm!

264
00:14:01,580 --> 00:14:02,680
Sarm!

265
00:14:02,930 --> 00:14:04,160
Sarm!!

266
00:14:08,050 --> 00:14:09,270
Sarm...

267
00:14:10,260 --> 00:14:11,260
Damn it.

268
00:14:16,590 --> 00:14:17,680
Sarm!

269
00:14:19,680 --> 00:14:21,670
Sarm, you're gone?!

270
00:14:23,680 --> 00:14:25,400
It's too soon, please!

271
00:14:26,120 --> 00:14:27,560
What are you doing here?

272
00:14:29,370 --> 00:14:30,320
Sarm.

273
00:14:30,440 --> 00:14:31,600
You were gone!

274
00:14:31,640 --> 00:14:33,920
I came to bring you your lunchbox,
but you weren't home.

275
00:14:33,960 --> 00:14:35,200
So I followed you here.

276
00:14:40,180 --> 00:14:41,720
I'm worried about you.

277
00:14:42,300 --> 00:14:43,000
Let go, Lantao.

278
00:14:43,110 --> 00:14:43,880
I refuse!

279
00:14:44,300 --> 00:14:44,840
I told you to let go.

280
00:14:44,920 --> 00:14:45,880
- No!
- Hm?

281
00:14:45,980 --> 00:14:46,920
I said, "Let go."

282
00:14:47,000 --> 00:14:47,680
Never!

283
00:14:48,830 --> 00:14:49,880
"Hands off," I said!

284
00:14:49,970 --> 00:14:50,620
No!

285
00:14:50,650 --> 00:14:51,160
Let go.

286
00:14:51,200 --> 00:14:51,680
I won't!

287
00:14:51,820 --> 00:14:52,350
Let go of me.

288
00:14:52,390 --> 00:14:52,760
Never!

289
00:14:52,790 --> 00:14:53,970
- Hands off!
- I said no!

290
00:15:07,500 --> 00:15:09,120
I didn't mean it.

291
00:15:13,260 --> 00:15:15,080
Sarm, wait for me, please!

292
00:15:16,760 --> 00:15:17,760
Sarm!

293
00:15:18,080 --> 00:15:19,580
Wait for me, please!

294
00:15:23,670 --> 00:15:24,670
Sarm.

295
00:15:25,980 --> 00:15:27,070
Sarm.

296
00:15:29,280 --> 00:15:30,200
Lantao.

297
00:15:30,290 --> 00:15:31,660
I brought you food.

298
00:15:33,300 --> 00:15:34,320
Go home already.

299
00:15:34,770 --> 00:15:35,800
Your dad's worried about you.

300
00:15:35,860 --> 00:15:36,690
I refuse.

301
00:15:36,830 --> 00:15:38,000
Just go ahead and take a shower.

302
00:15:38,050 --> 00:15:39,130
Do you have any idea that

303
00:15:39,150 --> 00:15:41,240
you are bothering me?!

304
00:15:47,320 --> 00:15:48,560
And I'm slightly annoyed.

305
00:15:49,660 --> 00:15:50,720
Sarm, you're one big meanie!

306
00:15:56,580 --> 00:15:57,680
Can't I just be in peace?

307
00:15:57,820 --> 00:15:59,180
I got interrupted
while relaxing in the sea.

308
00:15:59,470 --> 00:16:01,040
I didn't even get to drink my pain away.

309
00:16:01,570 --> 00:16:05,360
This sucks!

310
00:16:10,240 --> 00:16:11,350
[Ms. Namnueng's wedding is only 14 days away]

311
00:16:11,390 --> 00:16:12,480
It's been four days,

312
00:16:13,490 --> 00:16:15,410
and I haven't made any progress.

313
00:16:15,690 --> 00:16:17,880
Am I ChatGPT to him or what?

314
00:16:30,310 --> 00:16:33,380
Today, I'm here in Pak Chong District

315
00:16:33,470 --> 00:16:35,950
because I'm meeting a handsome man

316
00:16:35,980 --> 00:16:37,400
who has captured

317
00:16:37,440 --> 00:16:40,180
everyone's heart.

318
00:16:40,210 --> 00:16:41,540
This person

319
00:16:41,620 --> 00:16:44,240
is the owner of the gigantic Adisuan Farm,

320
00:16:44,500 --> 00:16:46,270
which is known for its accommodation,

321
00:16:46,300 --> 00:16:47,890
restaurants,
attractions, and activities.

322
00:16:47,920 --> 00:16:50,450
It covers the full spectrum of both agriculture

323
00:16:50,490 --> 00:16:52,350
and tourism businesses.

324
00:16:52,390 --> 00:16:53,560
And this person

325
00:16:53,880 --> 00:16:55,580
is right here. It's Mr. Sarm,

326
00:16:55,620 --> 00:16:57,980
Traiphop Adisuan!

327
00:16:59,660 --> 00:17:01,170
Remember my name

328
00:17:01,590 --> 00:17:03,770
because my golden era is here.

329
00:17:04,250 --> 00:17:05,319
And my slogan is...

330
00:17:05,420 --> 00:17:06,079
"Mighty

331
00:17:06,480 --> 00:17:07,280
and glorious.

332
00:17:07,390 --> 00:17:08,119
It's Traiphop."

333
00:17:10,440 --> 00:17:11,359
Alright...

334
00:17:11,990 --> 00:17:13,670
That introduction

335
00:17:13,710 --> 00:17:16,280
was totally grand and unforgettable.

336
00:17:16,310 --> 00:17:16,780
Yes.

337
00:17:16,810 --> 00:17:19,180
You're still as friendly as you've always been.

338
00:17:19,210 --> 00:17:19,800
Of course.

339
00:17:19,829 --> 00:17:22,859
If that is the case, I would like you

340
00:17:22,970 --> 00:17:25,160
to give us a tour of Adisuan Farm
if you don't mind.

341
00:17:25,490 --> 00:17:26,450
With pleasure, really.

342
00:17:26,619 --> 00:17:29,200
I'll show you
every nook and cranny of this place.

343
00:17:29,310 --> 00:17:30,200
But first,

344
00:17:30,290 --> 00:17:31,720
"An army marches on its stomach."

345
00:17:31,880 --> 00:17:33,160
I am going to take you

346
00:17:33,190 --> 00:17:34,470
to try exquisite dishes

347
00:17:34,500 --> 00:17:36,670
at our country-style garden restaurant.

348
00:17:36,880 --> 00:17:37,520
Our restaurant

349
00:17:37,580 --> 00:17:39,160
offers dishes...

350
00:17:39,460 --> 00:17:40,460
of the finest quality.

351
00:17:40,920 --> 00:17:43,120
The meat we serve is from our very own farm.

352
00:17:43,270 --> 00:17:44,680
The quality of the meat goes without saying.

353
00:17:44,720 --> 00:17:45,680
Because it's premium quality?

354
00:17:45,740 --> 00:17:46,680
It's good old local meat.

355
00:17:46,710 --> 00:17:48,330
- Huh...
- Mm.

356
00:17:48,710 --> 00:17:51,840
If I have to guess, the meat
must be very tender, correct?

357
00:17:51,880 --> 00:17:54,290
Well, you can already tell without having a bite.

358
00:17:54,330 --> 00:17:56,560
Whoa, is it because it melts in the mouth?

359
00:17:56,590 --> 00:17:58,470
- It melts before you get to eat it.
- Huh...

360
00:17:58,900 --> 00:17:59,520
Okay.

361
00:17:59,550 --> 00:18:01,700
Mr. Sarm, you are quite comedic yourself.

362
00:18:01,740 --> 00:18:02,880
Just keeping it casual.

363
00:18:03,090 --> 00:18:04,480
I have heard that

364
00:18:04,500 --> 00:18:06,270
you also sell fresh meat directly from the farm?

365
00:18:06,300 --> 00:18:06,540
Indeed.

366
00:18:06,580 --> 00:18:09,220
If our viewers at home

367
00:18:09,250 --> 00:18:10,710
would like to recreate your dishes,

368
00:18:10,750 --> 00:18:11,920
do you keep your recipes a secret?

369
00:18:12,520 --> 00:18:14,520
Do I? Well, I don't.

370
00:18:14,650 --> 00:18:16,640
But we really can't give you our recipes.

371
00:18:17,380 --> 00:18:18,160
Why is that, you may ask?

372
00:18:18,210 --> 00:18:18,920
Because...

373
00:18:18,980 --> 00:18:19,760
"our dishes are tasty

374
00:18:19,890 --> 00:18:21,160
'cause we forgot the recipes."

375
00:18:22,040 --> 00:18:23,240
- Alright.
- Right.

376
00:18:23,700 --> 00:18:26,570
Today, you're going to give us
a tour of Adisuan Farm,

377
00:18:26,600 --> 00:18:30,520
stretching across three districts
in Nakhon Ratchasima.

378
00:18:30,610 --> 00:18:33,340
The orange orchard takes up
70 percent of the entire land.

379
00:18:33,370 --> 00:18:35,650
It's as far as the eye can see,

380
00:18:35,740 --> 00:18:39,360
surrounded by overlapping mountain ranges.

381
00:18:39,480 --> 00:18:41,960
You can see

382
00:18:41,980 --> 00:18:44,120
how far he has taken the farm.

383
00:18:44,160 --> 00:18:45,870
- Right.
- Working this hard,

384
00:18:45,910 --> 00:18:47,260
do you even have time to rest at all?

385
00:18:48,210 --> 00:18:49,210
I'm a human, alright?

386
00:18:49,390 --> 00:18:50,450
Of course, I need some rest.

387
00:18:50,490 --> 00:18:51,740
Mm.

388
00:18:51,800 --> 00:18:55,070
Between the mountains and the beach,

389
00:18:55,570 --> 00:18:57,590
where would you rather spend your time off?

390
00:18:59,000 --> 00:19:00,080
I prefer the beach.

391
00:19:00,300 --> 00:19:01,640
It is, without a doubt, the beach

392
00:19:04,180 --> 00:19:04,970
because...

393
00:19:05,780 --> 00:19:07,210
when I was little,

394
00:19:08,950 --> 00:19:10,760
I would often spend time with my mother

395
00:19:10,790 --> 00:19:12,780
in her hometown in Chon Buri
during school breaks.

396
00:19:16,170 --> 00:19:17,170
Whenever...

397
00:19:17,660 --> 00:19:20,680
I need time to think
or deal with what's on my mind,

398
00:19:22,170 --> 00:19:23,660
I go to the beach.

399
00:19:29,770 --> 00:19:31,480
And the beach at night, in particular,

400
00:19:31,570 --> 00:19:32,680
is my absolute favorite.

401
00:19:33,970 --> 00:19:34,970
It's peaceful.

402
00:19:35,820 --> 00:19:38,390
Do you go there with your sweetheart?

403
00:19:38,430 --> 00:19:39,120
Oh.

404
00:19:39,300 --> 00:19:40,480
"I'm single...

405
00:19:40,580 --> 00:19:41,380
but not completely."

406
00:19:41,480 --> 00:19:42,670
Oh...

407
00:19:42,870 --> 00:19:44,570
This means that...

408
00:19:44,600 --> 00:19:46,140
you do have someone in your heart, correct?

409
00:19:47,520 --> 00:19:48,520
You can say that, yes.

410
00:19:49,710 --> 00:19:51,570
Alright, everyone.

411
00:19:51,860 --> 00:19:53,810
Alright, that was a nice little introduction

412
00:19:53,840 --> 00:19:55,960
to Mr. Sarm, Traiphop Adisuan.

413
00:19:55,990 --> 00:19:57,460
- Before we go, Mr. Sarm,
- Yes?

414
00:19:57,490 --> 00:20:00,130
could you leave a piece of advice

415
00:20:00,170 --> 00:20:03,170
for the passionate young people
watching us right now?

416
00:20:03,570 --> 00:20:04,490
No problem.

417
00:20:05,150 --> 00:20:06,360
"You catch more flies

418
00:20:06,400 --> 00:20:07,560
with a net than with honey."

419
00:20:18,770 --> 00:20:19,770
"I'm single...

420
00:20:19,800 --> 00:20:20,720
but not completely."

421
00:20:21,480 --> 00:20:23,190
This means that...

422
00:20:23,220 --> 00:20:24,990
you do have someone in your heart, correct?

423
00:20:29,670 --> 00:20:30,780
You can say that, yes.

424
00:20:40,000 --> 00:20:41,590
It is but a minor injury...

425
00:20:42,770 --> 00:20:43,770
like being stung by ants.

426
00:20:48,730 --> 00:20:49,730
You think we're friends?

427
00:20:51,100 --> 00:20:52,200
That's ridiculous.

428
00:20:53,130 --> 00:20:54,220
What's really wrong with you?

429
00:20:54,880 --> 00:20:56,370
Well, I'm officially heartbroken.

430
00:20:58,580 --> 00:21:01,760
Where is he crying his eyes out right now, I wonder?

431
00:21:09,160 --> 00:21:10,590
[I may disappear for a while.
No need to look for me.

432
00:21:10,620 --> 00:21:12,120
This wounded tiger needs time
to nurse his wounds. I will return when I am fine.]

433
00:21:12,150 --> 00:21:15,090
This wounded tiger
needs time to nurse his wounds?

434
00:21:19,990 --> 00:21:22,070
To know more about this wounded tiger...

435
00:21:24,590 --> 00:21:26,490
I need to enter its cave, don't I?

436
00:21:27,180 --> 00:21:29,780
My mission to bring
the teeny-tiny tiger back home

437
00:21:30,310 --> 00:21:32,020
has begun!

438
00:21:35,100 --> 00:21:36,570
No matter where you are hiding,

439
00:21:37,040 --> 00:21:39,320
I'm coming to bring you home.

440
00:22:25,320 --> 00:22:26,280
Dad.

441
00:22:26,660 --> 00:22:27,580
Mom.

442
00:22:29,170 --> 00:22:31,800
I'm leaving for work.

443
00:22:32,070 --> 00:22:34,680
Please wish me smooth sailing.

444
00:23:39,090 --> 00:23:41,470
Where on earth is
the Human Resources headquarters?

445
00:23:43,010 --> 00:23:43,810
Oh.

446
00:23:44,450 --> 00:23:45,390
Jam.

447
00:23:47,510 --> 00:23:48,760
Hello, Dr. Song.

448
00:23:48,800 --> 00:23:49,570
Hello.

449
00:23:50,370 --> 00:23:52,880
You can simply call me by my name.

450
00:23:53,470 --> 00:23:54,590
Would it be okay?

451
00:23:54,810 --> 00:23:55,760
Of course, it would.

452
00:23:56,070 --> 00:23:56,890
Well...

453
00:23:57,170 --> 00:24:00,840
I don't see you as Sib's assistant,

454
00:24:00,880 --> 00:24:03,570
but as PiMai's friend.

455
00:24:03,970 --> 00:24:05,880
Just address me

456
00:24:06,000 --> 00:24:07,680
the same way he does,

457
00:24:08,400 --> 00:24:09,280
okay?

458
00:24:11,880 --> 00:24:12,770
Right.

459
00:24:13,970 --> 00:24:14,970
Excellent.

460
00:24:15,730 --> 00:24:16,580
Now, then...

461
00:24:16,670 --> 00:24:17,940
What are you doing here?

462
00:24:19,940 --> 00:24:22,600
I've actually been wanting to meet you, Dr. Song.

463
00:24:22,880 --> 00:24:26,230
Mr. Sib tasked me with bringing Mr. Sarm home.

464
00:24:26,270 --> 00:24:29,120
That is why I want to talk to someone close to him.

465
00:24:29,370 --> 00:24:31,280
Did you read his note?

466
00:24:32,470 --> 00:24:34,100
Mm, yeah.

467
00:24:34,340 --> 00:24:38,680
I didn't expect him to fall for PiMai this much.

468
00:24:39,020 --> 00:24:42,400
By the way,
how exactly are you going to look for him?

469
00:24:42,630 --> 00:24:44,080
I'm not sure.

470
00:24:44,280 --> 00:24:45,670
But I started by

471
00:24:45,890 --> 00:24:48,040
hiring a private investigator.

472
00:24:48,600 --> 00:24:50,400
And the report just came in.

473
00:24:50,450 --> 00:24:53,360
It appears that Mr. Sarm hasn't left the country.

474
00:24:55,480 --> 00:24:58,260
Do you have ways to contact him, Dr. Song?

475
00:25:01,380 --> 00:25:02,380
Someone like Sarm

476
00:25:02,470 --> 00:25:05,400
cuts off all communication, Jam.

477
00:25:05,870 --> 00:25:07,570
He's actually isolating himself for real.

478
00:25:08,350 --> 00:25:09,940
Mm, though...

479
00:25:09,980 --> 00:25:11,570
I do understand him.

480
00:25:11,970 --> 00:25:13,570
It's his first heartbreak,

481
00:25:14,510 --> 00:25:15,680
so it hurts a fair bit.

482
00:25:16,570 --> 00:25:17,860
Mm...

483
00:25:21,300 --> 00:25:22,490
Dr. Song,

484
00:25:23,780 --> 00:25:26,800
is it possible for me
to meet Mr. Sarm's assistant?

485
00:25:29,060 --> 00:25:30,060
Sarm

486
00:25:30,370 --> 00:25:31,760
doesn't have an assistant.

487
00:25:32,170 --> 00:25:34,860
He hates being nagged.

488
00:25:35,110 --> 00:25:37,200
He manages everything himself.

489
00:25:37,270 --> 00:25:40,360
But if you want to get
an overview of Adisuan Farm,

490
00:25:40,580 --> 00:25:42,270
I'll take you to Thee.

491
00:25:42,440 --> 00:25:43,770
Mr. Thee?

492
00:25:43,960 --> 00:25:46,080
He's the general manager of this farm.

493
00:25:46,360 --> 00:25:48,360
Has he been working here for long?

494
00:25:48,470 --> 00:25:49,470
Well...

495
00:25:49,760 --> 00:25:51,870
It was when Sarm came back from his studies

496
00:25:51,930 --> 00:25:53,240
that Thee started working here.

497
00:25:53,370 --> 00:25:56,040
He is Sib's cousin, around the same age.

498
00:25:57,480 --> 00:25:58,880
Speaking of Thee,

499
00:25:59,430 --> 00:26:00,470
a few days ago,

500
00:26:00,570 --> 00:26:03,080
he almost got into a fight with Sib.

501
00:26:03,690 --> 00:26:04,550
Fortunately...

502
00:26:04,580 --> 00:26:06,440
Sib had an urgent trip to Chiang Mai.

503
00:26:06,720 --> 00:26:07,880
So nothing happened.

504
00:26:08,270 --> 00:26:09,760
Why were they fighting?

505
00:26:10,000 --> 00:26:11,060
At that time,

506
00:26:11,270 --> 00:26:13,850
Sib sent someone to audit the accounts,

507
00:26:14,000 --> 00:26:16,160
and Thee was very upset,

508
00:26:16,370 --> 00:26:18,240
seeing that as an interference with his work.

509
00:26:18,480 --> 00:26:20,560
Actually, it is hard to say

510
00:26:20,640 --> 00:26:22,670
because several years ago,

511
00:26:22,700 --> 00:26:24,280
this place almost didn't make it.

512
00:26:24,680 --> 00:26:26,080
They needed Sib

513
00:26:26,160 --> 00:26:27,760
to be their lifeline for years.

514
00:26:27,790 --> 00:26:29,300
It was when Sarm returned

515
00:26:29,380 --> 00:26:30,760
that the business flourished once more.

516
00:26:32,190 --> 00:26:33,460
Sarm, oh, Sarm.

517
00:26:33,570 --> 00:26:34,600
Just because he disappeared,

518
00:26:34,750 --> 00:26:36,120
everything got chaotic.

519
00:26:36,950 --> 00:26:39,890
Based on my twin sense,

520
00:26:40,180 --> 00:26:41,980
I'm guessing that

521
00:26:42,390 --> 00:26:44,060
he's probably taking some time off,

522
00:26:44,160 --> 00:26:46,780
getting stung by jellyfish on some beach.

523
00:26:47,860 --> 00:26:49,040
On some beach?

524
00:26:49,290 --> 00:26:50,360
That's my two cents.

525
00:26:50,640 --> 00:26:52,520
It has to be a beach in Thailand, too,

526
00:26:53,320 --> 00:26:54,480
as right now,

527
00:26:55,080 --> 00:26:56,720
Father is sick.

528
00:26:56,890 --> 00:26:58,300
So it's unlikely for him to leave the country.

529
00:26:59,250 --> 00:27:01,560
A beach in Thailand...

530
00:27:04,680 --> 00:27:07,280
Or is he residing at a vacation house in Chon Buri?

531
00:27:08,360 --> 00:27:09,640
Definitely not.

532
00:27:09,670 --> 00:27:12,550
Sarm is an extremist.

533
00:27:12,580 --> 00:27:14,750
When he does something,
he always goes all out.

534
00:27:14,970 --> 00:27:16,360
And when he wants to run away,

535
00:27:16,390 --> 00:27:18,280
he'll run away as far as he can go.

536
00:27:18,480 --> 00:27:19,360
This means that

537
00:27:19,550 --> 00:27:21,640
Chon Buri and Hua Hin are out of the equation.

538
00:27:25,820 --> 00:27:28,000
So that leaves the beaches in the South, then.

539
00:27:28,870 --> 00:27:29,800
Would you believe

540
00:27:29,850 --> 00:27:31,760
that I can tell what task Sib will give you

541
00:27:31,910 --> 00:27:33,200
once you manage

542
00:27:33,460 --> 00:27:35,800
to bring Sarm back?

543
00:27:36,070 --> 00:27:37,320
What task will it be?

544
00:27:37,880 --> 00:27:40,360
He probably has you stay at the farm.

545
00:27:40,490 --> 00:27:41,560
It's to...

546
00:27:41,860 --> 00:27:43,930
bring faith back to the workers

547
00:27:43,970 --> 00:27:47,920
and restore the tarnished image of Sarm.

548
00:27:50,970 --> 00:27:52,240
Don't stress out, Jam.

549
00:27:53,710 --> 00:27:54,230
Right.

550
00:27:54,260 --> 00:27:56,080
We lost track of time while chatting.

551
00:27:56,160 --> 00:27:57,960
Please come have some food with me.

552
00:27:58,040 --> 00:28:00,480
I just came back from the hospital,

553
00:28:00,640 --> 00:28:01,680
and I'm starving.

554
00:28:01,740 --> 00:28:03,780
I could eat a horse right now.

555
00:28:04,410 --> 00:28:06,790
Fortunately, that stupid horse
is nursing his broken heart.

556
00:28:06,820 --> 00:28:08,600
Otherwise, he would've been done for.

557
00:28:08,810 --> 00:28:09,280
I'll join you.

558
00:28:09,390 --> 00:28:10,090
Let's go.

559
00:28:10,580 --> 00:28:11,280
Right.

560
00:28:36,000 --> 00:28:37,200
Hello, Father.

561
00:28:37,320 --> 00:28:38,560
Oh, hello.

562
00:28:42,170 --> 00:28:43,780
This is Jam,

563
00:28:43,930 --> 00:28:45,460
Sib's assistant.

564
