Watch your tongue.

846
00:41:30,860 --> 00:41:31,710
Don't push your luck, Snoop.

847
00:41:31,740 --> 00:41:32,850
Do you think we're friends?

848
00:41:32,990 --> 00:41:35,450
Last I checked, I don't work for you.

849
00:41:35,540 --> 00:41:36,790
And even if I did...

850
00:41:36,810 --> 00:41:39,640
you have no right to say
such vile things to me.

851
00:41:40,060 --> 00:41:41,350
You threw rocks at me,

852
00:41:41,390 --> 00:41:42,580
so I threw the rocks back,

853
00:41:42,610 --> 00:41:44,240
not some beautiful flowers.

854
00:41:44,500 --> 00:41:45,720
Perhaps...

855
00:41:46,000 --> 00:41:47,440
I should call you...

856
00:41:47,540 --> 00:41:50,120
"Sarmonkey?"

857
00:41:50,330 --> 00:41:51,260
Sarmonkey?

858
00:41:51,910 --> 00:41:52,880
You called him a monkey?

859
00:41:53,810 --> 00:41:55,360
Why did you call him that?

860
00:41:55,420 --> 00:41:57,070
The last guy who said that didn't end well.

861
00:41:57,690 --> 00:41:59,800
And the ones
who said bad things to me

862
00:42:00,190 --> 00:42:02,960
are now recovering in the ICU.

863
00:42:04,490 --> 00:42:05,280
Wait...

864
00:42:05,810 --> 00:42:07,760
Still talking this much
even after I ripped your mouth?

865
00:42:07,970 --> 00:42:09,060
Next time we meet,

866
00:42:09,400 --> 00:42:10,960
I'll make sure you can't talk.

867
00:42:11,100 --> 00:42:12,400
You're all bark and no bite.

868
00:42:13,090 --> 00:42:14,160
Let me tell you something.

869
00:42:14,600 --> 00:42:15,730
You got away this time

870
00:42:15,810 --> 00:42:17,120
because I let you go.

871
00:42:17,180 --> 00:42:18,380
If I had chosen not to,

872
00:42:18,420 --> 00:42:19,750
you wouldn't have slipped away.

873
00:42:19,780 --> 00:42:20,490
Do you think prey

874
00:42:20,520 --> 00:42:22,200
can escape the claws of this mighty tiger?

875
00:42:22,240 --> 00:42:23,040
Roar!

876
00:42:29,810 --> 00:42:30,810
Who's that, Mister?

877
00:42:32,840 --> 00:42:33,840
My older brother's assistant.

878
00:42:33,940 --> 00:42:34,820
He's here to bring me home.

879
00:42:34,860 --> 00:42:36,470
You're going home already, Sarm?

880
00:42:36,760 --> 00:42:39,220
As long as my heart isn't healed,
I'm not going anywhere.

881
00:42:40,010 --> 00:42:41,130
It seems like

882
00:42:41,450 --> 00:42:43,610
a lot of people
have been looking for you lately.

883
00:42:43,900 --> 00:42:45,410
Don't tell me that guy...

884
00:42:45,440 --> 00:42:46,410
And you said it was over.

885
00:42:46,420 --> 00:42:48,030
Don't let me find you.
Where the hell are you?

886
00:42:48,350 --> 00:42:49,010
Huh?

887
00:42:49,310 --> 00:42:51,410
You want your fate to end at a hospital?

888
00:42:51,530 --> 00:42:52,620
- It's not him.
- What?

889
00:42:53,520 --> 00:42:55,520
Then who?

890
00:42:56,610 --> 00:42:57,610
It's whatever, then.

891
00:42:58,030 --> 00:42:59,530
I don't really care anyway.

892
00:42:59,960 --> 00:43:01,240
I'm leaving to see Ghibli.

893
00:43:01,320 --> 00:43:02,320
I miss Ghibli.

894
00:43:02,770 --> 00:43:03,810
Wait, Sarm!

895
00:43:05,360 --> 00:43:06,220
What is it?

896
00:43:06,420 --> 00:43:09,000
You looked really cool.

897
00:43:09,220 --> 00:43:11,010
You're certainly the king of all tigers.

898
00:43:12,520 --> 00:43:13,430
You have a good eye.

899
00:43:14,710 --> 00:43:15,430
I'll be going now.

900
00:43:24,520 --> 00:43:35,900
[Mission: Hunt Down the Teeny-tiny Tiger]

901
00:43:36,860 --> 00:43:40,190
My mission has officially begun.

902
00:43:40,380 --> 00:43:43,990
Now, I know that Mr. Sarm didn't disappear
just to leave everything behind.

903
00:43:44,540 --> 00:43:47,280
Instead, he's running away from his heart.

904
00:43:48,020 --> 00:43:52,110
What I just learned is that
he has cut himself off from everyone.

905
00:43:52,170 --> 00:43:54,950
He hasn't returned home or to the farm.

906
00:43:54,980 --> 00:43:56,720
He doesn't want anyone
to look for him either.

907
00:43:56,970 --> 00:44:00,480
But at the same time,
his family is waiting for him,

908
00:44:00,540 --> 00:44:02,560
and so is the work he left behind.

909
00:44:02,590 --> 00:44:05,790
Many people are waiting for his return.

910
00:44:07,100 --> 00:44:10,310
The only clue I had was the beach,

911
00:44:10,650 --> 00:44:14,700
as he'd always go there
to heal his broken heart.

912
00:44:14,800 --> 00:44:19,570
I have no idea if this trip will end with me
being able to bring Mr. Sarm home

913
00:44:19,700 --> 00:44:25,550
or becoming the one
who mends the heart of this "wounded tiger."

914
00:44:25,620 --> 00:44:27,910
I have found Mr. Sarm. He is on Ko Pha-ngan.

915
00:44:28,250 --> 00:44:29,580
It's time to end this mission

916
00:44:29,630 --> 00:44:32,340
by bringing the teeny-tiny tiger home.

917
00:44:34,860 --> 00:44:35,490
I'm not returning.

918
00:44:36,040 --> 00:44:37,800
Please, Mr. Sarm.

919
00:44:38,790 --> 00:44:40,490
If you do, my mission will be complete.

920
00:44:40,530 --> 00:44:42,170
If you are not coming home today,

921
00:44:42,210 --> 00:44:43,310
then when are you going to?

922
00:44:44,010 --> 00:44:44,930
Hey, hey.

923
00:44:45,130 --> 00:44:46,130
It's damn near impossible...

924
00:44:46,220 --> 00:44:47,220
to track you down,

925
00:44:47,660 --> 00:44:48,920
Mr. Sarm.

926
00:44:51,070 --> 00:44:55,760
♫I'm here to love you as myself,
not as a surrogate♫

927
00:44:55,790 --> 00:44:59,480
♫Let me be your safe space
when you need a break♫

928
00:44:59,510 --> 00:45:04,560
♫Who cares if I'm not your first or second?♫

929
00:45:04,600 --> 00:45:08,690
♫At least being your third still counts♫

930
00:45:09,410 --> 00:45:14,040
♫I'm here to love you,
no matter who left you with heartache♫

931
00:45:14,080 --> 00:45:17,740
♫Just let me heal your heart,
lending you my aid♫

932
00:45:17,770 --> 00:45:22,890
♫Have faith and believe in love once more♫

933
00:45:22,910 --> 00:45:24,840
♫'Cause good love is your Lucky Third♫

934
00:45:24,870 --> 00:45:28,190
♫Your Third, can it be me, love?♫

935
00:45:41,240 --> 00:45:43,170
♫'Cause good love is your Lucky Third♫

936
00:45:43,190 --> 00:45:46,780
♫Your Third, can it be me, love?♫

937
00:45:47,010 --> 00:45:50,080
[Your Third Series]
